{%- comment -%}
  High-speed symmetric cryptography: the AES state, 4 x 4 bytes, and ShiftRows.
  Row r rotates left by r bytes (the arrows on the right are r cells long). The bytes that start in column 0 are solid;
  the one in row 1 carries the accent, so its wrap-around can be followed. Each row is clipped by its own nested <svg>,
  and holds its four bytes three times over, so the loop can slide it without a seam.
  Live: one ShiftRows per beat (diagrams.js, SCENES.accel).
  Parameters: live (hover | always | off), trigger (view | manual), detail ("full" shows the labels), class.
{%- endcomment -%}
<svg class="diagram diagram--accel{% if include.class %} {{ include.class }}{% endif %}" viewBox="0 0 320 180" data-kit="diagram" data-live="{{ include.live | default: 'hover' }}" data-trigger="{{ include.trigger | default: 'view' }}"{% if include.detail == 'full' %} data-detail="full"{% endif %} role="img" aria-label="The AES state as a four by four grid of bytes; in ShiftRows each row r rotates left by r bytes, so the first column spreads onto a diagonal." fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.25" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
  {%- comment -%} the state {%- endcomment %}
  <rect class="dg-h dg-d" style="--t: 0" pathLength="1" x="47" y="30" width="120" height="120"/>
  <g class="dg-h" style="--t: 0.1">
    <path class="dg-d" style="--k: 2" pathLength="1" d="M77 30V150"/>
    <path class="dg-d" style="--k: 4" pathLength="1" d="M107 30V150"/>
    <path class="dg-d" style="--k: 6" pathLength="1" d="M137 30V150"/>
